        "AttributeName": "OperatingModes_ChooseOperatingMode",
        "CurrentValue": null,
        "DefaultValue": "Efficiency_FavorPerformance",
        "DisplayName": "Choose Operating Mode",
        "DisplayOrder": 132,
        "GrayOut": false,
        "HelpText": "Select the operating mode based on your preference. Power savings and performance are also highly dependent on hardware and software running on the system. The selected operating mode will automatically change low-level settings per the mode selected and will not allow them to be changed individually. Switch to \"Custom\" to set low level settings individually. \"Efficiency \u2013 Favor Performance\" default operating mode is comparable to Intel's Optimized Power Mode (OPM). Note, for maximum performance on applications that don't utilize all CPU cores, it is best to select \"Maximum Performance\" first, then select \"Custom\" and enable C-states. Doing so will allow the active cores to achieve maximum turbo uplift. Alternatively, unused cores can be disabled under \"System Settings\" => \"Processor\" =>\"Cores in CPU Package\".",
        "Hidden": false,
        "MenuPath": "./OperatingModes/OperatingModes_OperatingModes",
        "ReadOnly": false,
        "ResetRequired": true,
